"Some souls are reborn not as people but as monsters; the gods call them Experiments."
"Each Experiment bears the [Experiment] Emblem, which it cannot explain to any monster."
"The [Experiment] Emblem keeps a dungeon from harming its bearer until the bearer attacks."
"Each Experiment has a patron god who watches it and spends divine resources on it."
"Gramps tests open-ended traits on his Experiments to see how outside factors grow them."
"Some Dungeon Masters also test Gramps' new traits on their minions."
"Known Experiments: a slime, a spider, a crab, a dragon and a blood troll."
"Most Experiments are Earth souls, but Syl, the slime, is a native soul of this world."
"Syl, a slime Experiment, was a noble prodigy with Dimension Magic in her last life."
"In that life Syl was a young man in the Renait Federation, the realm of The Capital."
"He had spent 1 point on noble birth, 1 on Prodigy and 3 to unlock Dimension Magic."
"His older brother, jealous of his showy legacy magic, poisoned his birthday cake."
"That poisoned death earned 0 points; the 5 he spent came from a grand life before it."
"Gramps put that soul into a blue slime on a slime farm at Stantondale, now Southbrook."
"Syl remembers nothing of her past life; she learned it only from Gramps."
"Gramps has given Syl a great many extra lives; he says her soul is special."
"Syl bears the [Unique] Emblem: no other slime is like her, and it foils soul prying."
"Vee is a spider Experiment from Earth under Mother; she recalls little and was unhappy there."
"Leon is a crab Experiment from Earth under Unc; he is British and thinks like a scientist."
"The dragon Experiment has already destroyed a dungeon, beating its master Juniper."
"The blood troll Experiment fell out with Syl long ago."
"Humanoid monsters that reach high levels become aware of the gods and fear erasure."
"Keldenar's Eye of Truth showed Syl to be a slime; the gods now blur many of her traits from it."
"Keldenar swore an oath before the gods to keep Syl's secret and never harm her."
"Syl, Vee and Leon now live on Tanglebay, an island in the Vaelyssan Sea."
"Keldenar has since made a new race of his own, as he long planned."
"Keldenar, king of Keld and a diamond-rank Golemancer, was reborn from Earth as a human."
"Keldenar wanted a dimensional affinity at rebirth but lacked the points for it."
"Keldenar plans to earn enough deeds to be reborn as a golem, a race he hopes to make."
